      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The test `testCollections360` is simple — it verifies that a `FilterListIterator` constructed with only a predicate (no underlying iterator) correctly returns `false` for both `hasNext()` and `hasPrevious()`. However, the class is cluttered with unused fields, setup/teardown, and helper methods, plus the test variables have cryptic generated names (`var7`, `var9`, `var13`, `var14`). I'll clean all of that up.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused fields, setup/teardown boilerplate, and helper methods, replaces the cryptic generated variable names (`var7`, `var9`, `var13`, `var14`) with descriptive ones (`emptyPredicates`, `neverMatchingPredicate`, `iteratorUnderHasNext`, `iteratorUnderHasPrevious`), and adds a concise Javadoc explaining the regression being tested — while preserving the exact same method calls and assertions."
